#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/public-comment.bpmn:128
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "public-comment-changesets reroute, or cs-committee: <TWG> — <why> on GitHub from a person in the committee or editor lane. Moves the change-set to another TWG review committee and records who, when, from, to and why on the change-set record, so re-ingesting comments never resets it. Person-only (userTask): agents cannot re-route a change-set on their own."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/public-comment.bpmn:116
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "public-comment-changesets seed / propose: the agent groups the comments to be weighed into change-sets, one per change the document may need, each a record under changesets/ with its requirements and members. A PROPOSAL: nothing is decided, no GitHub issue is opened, and a comment may sit in zero, one or several change-sets. The record is the only one; everything shown about a change-set is rendered from it. A comment that arrives later is triaged the same way (Tool review-log-watch, cs-requests.ts triage): the agent suggests an open change-set that shares its sections, or a new one, and the committees (TWG) of that change-set, as its own suggestion only; a person's Change Set (human) or TWG (human) on the review sheet always wins. How a change-set came about does not matter: people adjudicate it."
msgstr ""

